<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasdrubal Barca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">245–<a href="/years/207-bce">207 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasdrubal Barca was a Carthaginian general, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca">Hamilcar Barca</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>. He commanded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, where the Scipio brothers defeated him near Hibera in 215 BCE. In 208 BCE he left Iberia to join Hannibal in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> but was defeated and killed at the Metaurus in 207 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasdrubal-barca.jpg" alt="Hasdrubal Barca" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Ogre at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hasdrubal_coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
